[
  "Shot with a Canon EOS R5, 85mm f/1.8 lens. The two quesadillas are centered in the frame, cut into neat halves, displayed on two simple matte ceramic plates. One plate is in sharp focus in the immediate foreground, while the second is softly blurred behind it, capturing a realistic serving for two. The camera is positioned at a 3/4 overhead angle, showing the volume of the golden-brown, crispy whole-wheat tortillas. The interior filling is visible along the cut edges, revealing a creamy, off-white cannellini bean mash, vibrant green wilted spinach, small pink chunks of shrimp, and salty white crumbles of feta. The tortillas feature a slightly uneven, rustic golden-brown sear with subtle charred spots from the skillet. Lighting is soft, natural, and directional, coming from a window on the left, casting gentle shadows and highlighting the texture of the toasted dough and the sheen of a light brush of olive oil. The setting is a rustic, aged oak tabletop with a rumpled, neutral-colored linen napkin tucked partially beneath the front plate. Beside the plate, a few stray crumbles of feta and a couple of small, fresh spinach leaves are scattered naturally. A small, blurred ramekin containing a touch of extra dried oregano sits in the background. Photorealistic, not AI-generated looking. The scene reflects a home-cooked lunch: lived-in, warm, and authentic. There are slight imperfections, such as a tiny stray piece of shrimp near the plate edge and an asymmetric placement of the quesadilla wedges. No plastic sheen, no unnaturally smooth surfaces. Warm, golden-hour color temperature. No text, no watermark, no logo, no hands, no faces. Indistinguishable from professional editorial food photography."
]
